  "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)(\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{y}{2})]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}\u20610)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(0)) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{8}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
